      "severity": "should-fix",
      "summary": "Computed stream results are still copied into locale prose instead of supplied as message parameters. Aggregator's ready$ valueMessages at this location are plain keys whose English values are literal 'order 31: 3 findings from 3 reviewers' and 'order 32: 2 findings from 3 reviewers' (studyEip/en.json:147-148), duplicating the result gather computes. marbleValue (rxjs/marbles.ts:110-111) returns the declared message without using its raw value argument. The same concrete shape occurs in scan's notes.1/.4/.8 in studyRxjs/en.json, which hardcode the computed balances 15, 12, 16 and 14. This violates catalog-rules.md:87-88 (computed model numbers use placeholders) and :120 (worked arithmetic and narration use parameterized messages), within D042's shared narration repair. Current English defaults agree; the defect is the duplicated computed facts and missing changed-value regression, not a claim of a failing retained default test. The twice-report Aggregator spec already uses report/setSummary descriptors with params, while shipped defaults retain plain literal summaries. Use parameterized messages fed from the numeric/payload source, preserve raw executable payloads, and add a regression that changes computed values while retaining the same translation template and verifies both rendered values and unchanged mechanism semantics.",
